    <example number="7.61">
      <problem>
        <p>Factor completely: $$g^{3} + 25g$$.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="A step-by-step guide to factoring an algebraic expression, illustrating the process with questions, outcomes, and mathematical forms.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
              <cell>Yes, g.</cell>
              <cell>$$g^{3} + 25g$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$g\left( {g^{2} + 25} \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more than three terms?</cell>
              <cell>Binomial.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is it a sum ? Of squares?</cell>
              <cell>Yes.</cell>
              <cell>Sums of squares are prime.</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is the expression factored completely?</cell>
              <cell>Yes.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.$$\begin{array}{l} \\ \\ \\ {\mspace{45mu} g\left( {g^{2} + 25} \right)} \\ {\mspace{45mu} g^{3} + 25g\ ✓} \end{array}$$</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
