    <example number="7.62">
      <problem>
        <p>Factor completely: $$12y^{2} - 75$$.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Detailed steps for factoring the algebraic expression 12y^2 - 75, showing identification of GCF and difference of squares.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
              <cell>Yes, 3.</cell>
              <cell>$$12y^{2} - 75$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$3\left( {4y^{2} - 25} \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more than three terms?</cell>
              <cell>Binomial.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is it a sum?</cell>
              <cell>No.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is it a difference? Of squares or cubes?</cell>
              <cell>Yes, squares.</cell>
              <cell>$$3\left( {\left( {2y} \right)^{2} - (5)^{2}} \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Write as a product of conjugates.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$3\left( {2y - 5} \right)\left( {2y + 5} \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is the expression factored completely?</cell>
              <cell>Yes.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Neither binomial is a difference of squares.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.$$\begin{array}{l} \\ \\ {\mspace{45mu} 3\left( {2y - 5} \right)\left( {2y + 5} \right)} \\ {\mspace{45mu} 3\left( {4y^{2} - 25} \right)} \\ {\mspace{45mu} 12y^{2} - 75\ ✓} \end{array}$$</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
