    <example number="7.65">
      <problem>
        <p>Factor completely: $$24x^{3} + 81$$.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
              <cell>Yes, 3.</cell>
              <cell>$$24x^{3} + 81$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor it out.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$3\left( 8x^{3} + 27 \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more than three terms?</cell>
              <cell>Binomial.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is it a sum or difference?</cell>
              <cell>Sum.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Of squares or cubes?</cell>
              <cell>Sum of cubes.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Write it using the sum of cubes pattern.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is the expression factored completely?</cell>
              <cell>Yes.</cell>
              <cell>$$3(2x + 3)\left( 4x^{2} - 6x + 9 \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check by multiplying.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>We leave the check to you.</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
