    <example number="7.67">
      <problem>
        <p>Factor completely: $$3x^{2} + 6bx - 3ax - 6ab$$.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="This table demonstrates the step-by-step process of factoring a polynomial expression by grouping, including GCF identification and checking the solution.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
              <cell>Yes, 3.</cell>
              <cell>$$3x^{2} + 6bx - 3ax - 6ab$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$3\left( {x^{2} + 2bx - ax - 2ab} \right)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more terms?</cell>
              <cell>More than 3 terms.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Use grouping.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\begin{matrix} \\ {3\left\lbrack {x\left( {x + 2b} \right) - a\left( {x + 2b} \right)} \right\rbrack} \\ {3\left( {x + 2b} \right)\left( {x - a} \right)} \end{matrix}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check your answer.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is the expression factored completely? Yes.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.$$\begin{array}{l} \\ \\ {\mspace{54mu} 3\left( {x + 2b} \right)\left( {x - a} \right)} \\ {\mspace{54mu} 3\left( {x^{2} - ax + 2bx - 2ab} \right)} \\ {\mspace{54mu} 3x^{2} - 3ax + 6bx - 6ab\ ✓} \end{array}$$</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
