      <problem>
        <p>Watermelon drop A springtime tradition at the University of California San Diego is the Watermelon Drop, where a watermelon is dropped from the seventh story of Urey Hall.</p>
        <list type="ol" style="1">
          <item>ⓐ The binomial $$-16t^{2} + 80$$ gives the height of the watermelon $$t$$ seconds after it is dropped. Factor the greatest common factor from this binomial.</item>
          <item>ⓑ If the watermelon is thrown down with initial velocity 8 feet per second, its height after $$t$$ seconds is given by the trinomial $$-16t^{2} - 8t + 80$$. Completely factor this trinomial.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>ⓐ $$-16\left( {t^{2} - 5} \right)$$ ⓑ $$-8\left( {2t + 5} \right)\left( {t - 2} \right)$$</p>
      </solution>
